    </section>

    <section class="slide" data-title="Find the contradictions" aria-hidden="true">
      <div class="slide-inner">
        <header class="slide-header"><span class="eyebrow">CityU ethics application · consistency across files</span></header>
        <div data-language="en">
          <h2>The submitted files must agree</h2>
          <p class="source-context">The <a href="https://soe.cityu.edu.mo/en/notice/393" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">School’s application notice ↗</a> requires the form or statement alongside the proposal and research tools. Each pair below contains two equally important parts of that submission.</p>
          <div class="audit-grid">
            <details><summary><span class="audit-pair"><span class="audit-file"><strong>Application form</strong><span>“No identifiable data.”</span></span><span class="audit-file"><strong>Interview and recruitment plans</strong><span>Audio interviews and a named list.</span></span></span></summary><p>Audio and the list may identify participants. Explain separation, access and the precise meaning of any de-identification claim.</p></details>
            <details><summary><span class="audit-pair"><span class="audit-file"><strong>Application form</strong><span>“No foreseeable risk.”</span></span><span class="audit-file"><strong>Recruitment invitation</strong><span>The teacher invites their own students in class.</span></span></span></summary><p>Consider pressure, grades and relationships. Redesign the invitation and who sees participation decisions.</p></details>
            <details><summary><span class="audit-pair"><span class="audit-file"><strong>Consent sheet</strong><span>“Withdraw at any time.”</span></span><span class="audit-file"><strong>Analysis and publication plan</strong><span>Quotations are published after transcription.</span></span></span></summary><p>Give a realistic withdrawal procedure and explain the point after which removing data may no longer be possible.</p></details>
            <details><summary><span class="audit-pair"><span class="audit-file"><strong>Data management plan</strong><span>“Only researchers have access.”</span></span><span class="audit-file"><strong>Method protocol</strong><span>Third-party AI transcription is used.</span></span></span></summary><p>Identify the provider, transfer, settings, permission and any approved alternative before making the access claim.</p></details>
          </div>
          <p class="instruction"><strong>Pairs:</strong> name the contradiction, suggest a repair aloud, then open the explanation.</p>
        </div>
        <div data-language="zh" hidden lang="zh-Hant">
          <h2>提交的各份文件必須一致</h2>
          <p class="source-context"><a href="https://soe.cityu.edu.mo/en/notice/393" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">學院申請通知 ↗</a>要求同時提交申請表或聲明、研究計劃及研究工具。以下每組均由兩份同等重要的申請材料組成。</p>
          <div class="audit-grid">
            <details><summary><span class="audit-pair"><span class="audit-file"><strong>倫理申請表</strong><span>「不收集可識別資料。」</span></span><span class="audit-file"><strong>訪談與招募計劃</strong><span>錄音訪談及具名名單。</span></span></span></summary><p>錄音及名單可能識別參與者。須說明分隔、權限，以及「去識別」一詞的準確含義。</p></details>
            <details><summary><span class="audit-pair"><span class="audit-file"><strong>倫理申請表</strong><span>「沒有可預見風險。」</span></span><span class="audit-file"><strong>招募邀請函</strong><span>教師在課堂邀請自己的學生。</span></span></span></summary><p>考慮壓力、成績及關係；重新設計邀請方式及參與決定的知情範圍。</p></details>
            <details><summary><span class="audit-pair"><span class="audit-file"><strong>知情同意書</strong><span>「可隨時撤回。」</span></span><span class="audit-file"><strong>分析與發表計劃</strong><span>逐字稿引文將會發表。</span></span></span></summary><p>提供可執行的退出程序，並說明資料在甚麼階段可能已無法移除。</p></details>
            <details><summary><span class="audit-pair"><span class="audit-file"><strong>資料管理計劃</strong><span>「只有研究者可存取。」</span></span><span class="audit-file"><strong>研究方法方案</strong><span>使用第三方AI轉錄。</span></span></span></summary><p>在作出存取承諾前，辨明供應商、傳輸、設定、許可及已獲准的替代方案。</p></details>
          </div>
          <p class="instruction"><strong>兩人一組：</strong>先說出矛盾及一項修正，再打開說明。</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="slide consent-slide" data-title="Consent as an ongoing choice" aria-hidden="true">
      <div class="slide-inner">
        <header class="slide-header"><span class="eyebrow">ESRC and BERA · informed consent</span></header>
        <div data-language="en">
          <h2>Consent is an ongoing choice</h2>
          <p class="source-context"><a href="https://www.ukri.org/councils/esrc/guidance-for-applicants/research-ethics-guidance/consent/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">ESRC consent guidance ↗</a> calls for clear information, freedom from pressure and a choice people can revisit. <a href="https://www.bera.ac.uk/publication/ethical-guidelines-for-educational-research-fifth-edition-2024" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">BERA’s education guidelines ↗</a> apply these duties in research with learners.</p>
          <div class="consent-chain">
            <article><b>01</b><h3>Invitation</h3><p>Why me? Who asks? Can I take time?</p></article>
            <article><b>02</b><h3>Information</h3><p>What happens, for how long, and with which data?</p></article>
            <article><b>03</b><h3>Choice</h3><p>Can I refuse parts such as recording or future sharing?</p></article>
            <article><b>04</b><h3>Continuity</h3><p>Can I pause, skip, withdraw or ask later?</p></article>
          </div>
          <div class="consent-modes">
            <article><h3>Active consent · opt in</h3><p>A person affirmatively agrees after receiving information; record the choice. For minors, required guardian permission and the young person’s own agreement are separate decisions.</p></article>
            <article><h3>Passive consent · opt out</h3><p>A missing response is treated as permission after a notice. Silence may mean the notice was missed. This route needs explicit justification and prior approval under applicable rules.</p></article>
          </div>
          <p class="source-note">For the school study, obtain the required permission for interviews, drafts and AI logs through an affirmative choice. <a href="https://www.hhs.gov/ohrp/regulations-and-policy/guidance/faq/informed-consent/index.html" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">US OHRP’s parental-permission FAQ ↗</a> gives one jurisdiction-specific example; check the local review requirements.</p>
        </div>
        <div data-language="zh" hidden lang="zh-Hant">
          <h2>知情同意是持續的選擇</h2>
          <p class="source-context"><a href="https://www.ukri.org/councils/esrc/guidance-for-applicants/research-ethics-guidance/consent/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">ESRC知情同意指引 ↗</a>要求資訊清楚、參與不受壓力，並容許參與者重新考慮。<a href="https://www.bera.ac.uk/publication/ethical-guidelines-for-educational-research-fifth-edition-2024" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">BERA教育研究指引 ↗</a>把這些責任應用於學習者研究。</p>
          <div class="consent-chain">
            <article><b>01</b><h3>邀請</h3><p>為何邀請我？誰邀請？我可以考慮多久？</p></article>
            <article><b>02</b><h3>資訊</h3><p>要做甚麼、多久、涉及哪些資料？</p></article>
            <article><b>03</b><h3>選擇</h3><p>我可否拒絕錄音或日後分享等部分？</p></article>
            <article><b>04</b><h3>持續確認</h3><p>我可否暫停、跳題、退出或日後提問？</p></article>
          </div>
          <div class="consent-modes">
            <article><h3>主動同意 · 明確選擇參與</h3><p>知情後明確表示同意，並記錄決定。涉及未成年人時，按規定取得監護人許可，亦須分別取得年輕參與者自己的同意或贊同。</p></article>
            <article><h3>被動同意 · 未反對即視為同意</h3><p>發出通知後，把沒有回覆視為許可。沉默也可能表示未收到通知；採用此方式須提出明確理據，並事先符合適用規定及獲得批准。</p></article>
          </div>
          <p class="source-note">本例蒐集訪談、作文或AI使用紀錄前，須循明確選擇取得所需許可。<a href="https://www.hhs.gov/ohrp/regulations-and-policy/guidance/faq/informed-consent/index.html" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">美國OHRP家長許可問答 ↗</a>提供一個特定司法管轄區的例子；仍須核對本地審查規定。</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="slide" data-title="Spot the problem in consent text" aria-hidden="true">
      <div class="slide-inner">
        <header class="slide-header"><span class="eyebrow">Consent language · discuss and reveal</span></header>
        <div data-language="en">
          <h2>Which promises exceed this study’s safeguards?</h2>
          <blockquote class="flawed-text">“By signing, you agree to all activities and future uses. All data are anonymous. There are no risks. You can withdraw at any time.”</blockquote>
          <p class="instruction">Discuss how to describe recording, confidentiality and withdrawal more accurately. Then compare a possible revision.</p>
          <details class="reveal"><summary>Compare a possible revision</summary><p>“You may choose the writing activity separately from the interview and audio recording. We will remove names from the transcript. The research team can identify recordings while they are stored. In a small school, details in a published quotation may allow others to recognise a participant. You can request removal of your interview data until [a justified stage/date], before results are combined or published.” The actual study must fill and justify the bracketed limit.</p></details>
        </div>
        <div data-language="zh" hidden lang="zh-Hant">
          <h2>哪些承諾無法兌現？</h2>
          <blockquote class="flawed-text">「簽名即表示同意所有活動及日後用途。所有資料均匿名，研究沒有風險。你可隨時撤回。」</blockquote>
          <p class="instruction">討論如何更準確說明錄音、保密及退出，再比較一種可能的修訂。</p>
          <details class="reveal"><summary>比較一種可能的修訂</summary><p>「你可分別決定是否參與寫作活動、訪談及錄音。我們會從逐字稿移除姓名。研究團隊在保存期間仍可能透過錄音識別你。在規模較小的學校，發表引文中的細節也可能讓他人認出參與者。你可在〔須說明理由的階段／日期〕前要求移除訪談資料，之後資料可能已合併分析或發表。」實際研究須填寫並解釋方括號內限制。</p></details>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="slide" data-title="Trace risk through the study" aria-hidden="true">
      <div class="slide-inner">
        <header class="slide-header"><span class="eyebrow">ESRC / UKRI · risk and benefit</span></header>
        <div data-language="en">
          <h2>Risk includes social and reputational harm</h2>
          <p class="source-context">The <a href="https://www.ukri.org/councils/esrc/guidance-for-applicants/research-ethics-guidance/risk-and-benefit/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">ESRC risk and benefit guidance ↗</a> considers participants, wider groups and researchers. It asks for the likely scale of harm, expected benefit, safeguards and a response if harm occurs.</p>
          <div class="risk-equation"><span>Activity</span><b>→</b><span>Possible harm</span><b>→</b><span>Prevention</span><b>→</b><span>Response</span><b>→</b><span>Remaining risk</span></div>
          <div class="risk-grid">
            <article><h3>Social / educational</h3><p>A teacher knows who refused; a classroom group may infer who spoke.</p></article>
            <article><h3>Emotional</h3><p>An interview revisits conflict, failure or exclusion.</p></article>
            <article><h3>Privacy / reputation</h3><p>A quotation, voice or platform trace identifies a person or school.</p></article>
            <article><h3>Researcher / bystander</h3><p>A field visit or incidental recording affects people outside the intended sample.</p></article>
          </div>
          <p class="takeaway">Trace each risk from the activity through possible harm, prevention and response to the remaining risk.</p>
        </div>
        <div data-language="zh" hidden lang="zh-Hant">
          <h2>風險包括社會及聲譽傷害</h2>
          <p class="source-context"><a href="https://www.ukri.org/councils/esrc/guidance-for-applicants/research-ethics-guidance/risk-and-benefit/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">ESRC風險與益處指引 ↗</a>關注參與者、其他群體及研究者，要求考慮傷害的可能性與程度、預期益處、保障措施及發生傷害時的應對。</p>
          <div class="risk-equation"><span>活動</span><b>→</b><span>可能傷害</span><b>→</b><span>預防</span><b>→</b><span>應對</span><b>→</b><span>剩餘風險</span></div>
          <div class="risk-grid">
            <article><h3>社會／教育</h3><p>教師知道誰拒絕；班級可能推斷誰接受訪談。</p></article>
            <article><h3>情緒</h3><p>訪談觸及衝突、失敗或排斥經歷。</p></article>
            <article><h3>私隱／聲譽</h3><p>引文、聲音或平台痕跡識別個人或學校。</p></article>
            <article><h3>研究者／旁觀者</h3><p>田野工作或意外錄音影響原定樣本以外的人。</p></article>
          </div>
          <p class="takeaway">從研究活動開始，逐步說明可能傷害、預防措施、既定應對及剩餘風險。</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="slide" data-title="What would you do next?" aria-hidden="true">
      <div class="slide-inner">
        <header class="slide-header"><span class="eyebrow">Scenario triage · groups of three</span></header>
        <div data-language="en">
          <h2>Rehearse the response while the stakes are low.</h2>
          <div class="scenario-grid">
            <article><span>01 · Distress</span><p>An interviewee becomes upset and asks whether the recording can be erased.</p><details><summary>Discuss, then open</summary><p>Pause the interview, check the person’s choice and immediate needs, follow the approved support pathway, and explain the realistic withdrawal and deletion process. Record the incident through the agreed route.</p></details></article>
            <article><span>02 · Disclosure</span><p>A participant reports a serious safety concern after you promised “complete confidentiality.”</p><details><summary>Discuss, then open</summary><p>The promise was too broad. Follow the pre-agreed disclosure and safeguarding process, limit disclosure to people authorised to act, and explain limits to confidentiality at consent.</p></details></article>
            <article><span>03 · Scope change</span><p>A school offers additional attendance records after the study begins.</p><details><summary>Discuss, then open</summary><p>Before adding the dataset, check purpose, permission, participant information, data plan and whether review or amendment is needed before access or analysis.</p></details></article>
          </div>
          <p class="instruction">Choose one scenario to discuss, then reveal the suggested response.</p>
        </div>
        <div data-language="zh" hidden lang="zh-Hant">
          <h2>趁風險尚未發生，先演練應對。</h2>
          <div class="scenario-grid">
            <article><span>01 · 不適</span><p>受訪者感到難過，並問能否刪除錄音。</p><details><summary>先討論，再打開</summary><p>暫停訪談，了解參與者選擇與即時需要，依已批准的支援途徑處理，解釋可行的退出及刪除程序，並按既定路徑記錄事件。</p></details></article>
            <article><span>02 · 披露</span><p>參與者透露嚴重安全問題，而你曾承諾「完全保密」。</p><details><summary>先討論，再打開</summary><p>這項承諾過於絕對。依預先商定的披露及保障程序處理，只向有權採取行動的人披露，並在同意階段說明保密界限。</p></details></article>
            <article><span>03 · 範圍變更</span><p>研究開始後，學校提出提供額外的出席紀錄。</p><details><summary>先討論，再打開</summary><p>加入新資料前，先核對目的、許可、參與者資訊及資料計劃，並確定存取或分析前是否需修訂審查。</p></details></article>
          </div>
          <p class="instruction">選一個情境討論，再打開參考應對。</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="slide" data-title="Privacy, anonymity and confidentiality" aria-hidden="true">
      <div class="slide-inner">
        <header class="slide-header"><span class="eyebrow">ESRC / UKRI · privacy and confidentiality</span></header>
        <div data-language="en">
          <h2>Privacy, confidentiality, anonymity</h2>
          <p class="source-context">The <a href="https://www.ukri.org/councils/esrc/guidance-for-applicants/research-ethics-guidance/consent/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">ESRC consent guidance ↗</a> asks researchers to explain limits to confidentiality; its <a href="https://www.ukri.org/councils/esrc/guidance-for-applicants/research-ethics-guidance/risk-and-benefit/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">risk guidance ↗</a> asks who may be identifiable. The <a href="https://ico.org.uk/for-organisations/uk-gdpr-guidance-and-resources/data-sharing/anonymisation/introduction-to-anonymisation/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">ICO anonymisation guidance ↗</a> explains that data remain identifiable if the team can reconnect them to a person.</p>
          <div class="comparison">
            <article><span>Privacy</span><h3>Control over access</h3><p>Who is approached, observed or recorded, and in which setting?</p></article>
            <article><span>Confidentiality</span><h3>Control over disclosure</h3><p>Researchers restrict access to known identities and control what is published.</p></article>
            <article><span>Anonymity</span><h3>Identity remains untraceable</h3><p>After names are removed, a voice recording or a quotation about a distinctive classroom experience may still reveal the participant’s identity.</p></article>
          </div>
          <p class="instruction"><strong>Answer: “anonymous”.</strong> The team can identify the speaker by matching the recording to a name. The consent form should state who can access the identifiable recording and how it will be protected.</p>
        </div>
        <div data-language="zh" hidden lang="zh-Hant">
          <h2>私隱、保密與匿名</h2>
          <p class="source-context"><a href="https://www.ukri.org/councils/esrc/guidance-for-applicants/research-ethics-guidance/consent/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">ESRC知情同意指引 ↗</a>要求交代保密界限；<a href="https://www.ukri.org/councils/esrc/guidance-for-applicants/research-ethics-guidance/risk-and-benefit/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">風險指引 ↗</a>要求考慮誰可能被識別。<a href="https://ico.org.uk/for-organisations/uk-gdpr-guidance-and-resources/data-sharing/anonymisation/introduction-to-anonymisation/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">英國資料專員公署（ICO）的匿名化指引 ↗</a>指出，若團隊可把資料重新對應到個人，資料仍可識別。</p>
          <div class="comparison">
            <article><span>私隱</span><h3>控制接觸</h3><p>誰在甚麼場景被邀請、觀察或錄音？</p></article>
            <article><span>保密</span><h3>控制披露</h3><p>研究者掌握身份時，須限制查閱者及發表內容。</p></article>
            <article><span>匿名</span><h3>實際無法識別</h3><p>刪除姓名後，聲音或描述獨特課堂經歷的引文，仍可能使他人認出參與者。</p></article>
          </div>
          <p class="instruction"><strong>答案：「匿名」。</strong>團隊可把錄音對應到姓名，從而辨識說話者。同意書應說明誰可查閱這些可識別的錄音，以及如何保護錄音。</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="slide" data-title="Map the data lifecycle" aria-hidden="true">
      <div class="slide-inner">
        <header class="slide-header"><span class="eyebrow">ESRC / UKRI · research data requirements</span></header>
        <div data-language="en">
          <h2>Data management begins before collection</h2>
          <p class="source-context">For ESRC-funded work, <a href="https://www.ukri.org/councils/esrc/guidance-for-applicants/research-ethics-guidance/data-requirements/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">ESRC data requirements ↗</a> make curation, management and potential sharing part of the project itself. The interview-file route below makes those responsibilities concrete.</p>
          <div class="lifecycle-grid">
            {lifecycle.map((step) => <details><summary><b>{step.n}</b>{step.en}</summary><p>{step.qEn}</p></details>)}
          </div>
          <p class="instruction">Trace the route together. Notice when another person, device, service or file copy gains access.</p>
        </div>
        <div data-language="zh" hidden lang="zh-Hant">
          <h2>資料管理從蒐集前開始</h2>
          <p class="source-context">對ESRC資助的研究，<a href="https://www.ukri.org/councils/esrc/guidance-for-applicants/research-ethics-guidance/data-requirements/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">ESRC資料要求 ↗</a>把資料整理、管理及可能的分享視為研究本身的一部分。以下以一份訪談錄音說明這些責任。</p>
          <div class="lifecycle-grid">
            {lifecycle.map((step) => <details><summary><b>{step.n}</b>{step.zh}</summary><p>{step.qZh}</p></details>)}
          </div>
          <p class="instruction">一起追蹤資料路徑，留意何時有其他人、裝置、服務或檔案副本取得存取權。</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="slide" data-title="Contexts that change ethical decisions" aria-hidden="true">
      <div class="slide-inner">
        <header class="slide-header"><span class="eyebrow">BERA · insider teacher-researcher case</span></header>
        <div data-language="en">
          <h2>Roles and relationships change the decision</h2>
          <p class="source-context">In <a href="https://www.bera.ac.uk/publication/research-ethics-case-studies-2024-classroom-observation-for-insider-teacher-researchers" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">BERA’s 2024 insider-research case ↗</a>, a teacher observing a colleague must separate her research role from her everyday responsibilities. The same tension appears when teachers study their own students.</p>
          <div class="station-grid">
            <article><b>01</b><h3>Children and young people</h3><p>Whose permission and whose assent matter? How will refusal be recognised during an activity?</p></article>
            <article><b>02</b><h3>Dual roles</h3><p>When a researcher also teaches, grades or manages participants, can they freely refuse? Who recruits and sees the decision?</p></article>
            <article><b>03</b><h3>Conflicts of interest</h3><p>Could a funder, platform vendor, promotion goal or personal relationship affect design, analysis or reporting? What must be disclosed and managed?</p></article>
          </div>
          <p class="takeaway">Context shapes participant protection and the independence of the research record. Disclose competing interests; redesign roles or procedures when pressure persists.</p>
        </div>
        <div data-language="zh" hidden lang="zh-Hant">
          <h2>角色與關係改變倫理決策</h2>
          <p class="source-context">在<a href="https://www.bera.ac.uk/publication/research-ethics-case-studies-2024-classroom-observation-for-insider-teacher-researchers" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">BERA的2024年內部研究案例 ↗</a>中，教師觀察同事時須區分研究角色與日常職責。教師研究自己任教的學生時，同樣面對這種張力。</p>
          <div class="station-grid">
            <article><b>01</b><h3>兒童與青少年</h3><p>需要誰的許可及誰的同意參與？活動中如何辨認拒絕？</p></article>
            <article><b>02</b><h3>雙重角色</h3><p>研究者若同時任教、評分或管理參與者，對方能否自由拒絕？誰負責招募及知悉決定？</p></article>
            <article><b>03</b><h3>利益衝突</h3><p>資助者、平台供應商、晉升目標或私人關係會否影響設計、分析及報告？哪些利益須披露及管理？</p></article>
          </div>
          <p class="takeaway">研究情境影響參與者保障及研究紀錄的獨立性。應披露競爭利益；若壓力持續，就須調整角色或程序。</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

