    <section class="slide" data-title="Authorship and author order" aria-hidden="true">
      <div class="slide-inner">
        <header class="slide-header"><span class="eyebrow">ALLEA (2023) · publication and authorship</span></header>
        <div data-language="en">
          <h2>Authorship means credit and responsibility</h2>
          <p class="source-context">The <a href="https://allea.org/wp-content/uploads/2023/06/European-Code-of-Conduct-Revised-Edition-2023.pdf" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">ALLEA European Code of Conduct (2023) ↗</a> asks authors to agree on order, make significant contributions, approve the final work and accept responsibility. It also encourages contribution statements and credit for non-author help.</p>
          <div class="integrity-trio">
            <article><span>01 · Authorship</span><h3>Qualify for the byline</h3><p>Use the journal’s authorship criteria to assess each contribution. Providing access, funding or general supervision still requires a separate authorship decision.</p></article>
            <article><span>02 · Contribution</span><h3>Describe the work</h3><p>Record who designed, collected, analysed, drafted, revised and approved the work. Credit non-author help appropriately.</p></article>
            <article><span>03 · Order</span><h3>Agree and revisit</h3><p>Discuss author order early, revisit it when work changes, and obtain all authors’ agreement before submission.</p></article>
          </div>
          <p class="takeaway">A contribution statement makes work visible; the byline and its order remain decisions the authors must justify together.</p>
        </div>
        <div data-language="zh" hidden lang="zh-Hant">
          <h2>作者署名同時涉及肯定貢獻與承擔責任</h2>
          <p class="source-context"><a href="https://allea.org/wp-content/uploads/2023/06/European-Code-of-Conduct-Revised-Edition-2023.pdf" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">ALLEA《歐洲研究誠信行為守則》（2023）↗</a>要求作者商定次序、作出重要貢獻、批准最終稿並承擔責任；亦鼓勵提交貢獻聲明及肯定非作者的協助。</p>
          <div class="integrity-trio">
            <article><span>01 · 作者資格</span><h3>符合署名條件</h3><p>依目標期刊的作者準則評估各項貢獻。提供准入、經費或一般督導時，仍須另行判斷作者資格。</p></article>
            <article><span>02 · 貢獻</span><h3>說明實際工作</h3><p>記錄誰設計、蒐集、分析、撰寫、修訂及批准研究；以適當方式致謝非作者的協助。</p></article>
            <article><span>03 · 次序</span><h3>及早商議並重議</h3><p>及早討論作者次序；工作有變時重新商議；投稿前取得所有作者同意。</p></article>
          </div>
          <p class="takeaway">貢獻聲明讓工作可見；作者名單及次序仍須由作者共同論證。</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="slide" data-title="CRediT contributor roles" aria-hidden="true">
      <div class="slide-inner">
        <header class="slide-header"><span class="eyebrow">NISO CRediT · contributor role taxonomy</span></header>
        <div data-language="en">
          <h2>CRediT describes the work behind a paper</h2>
          <p class="source-context"><a href="https://credit.niso.org/contributor-roles-defined/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">NISO’s CRediT taxonomy ↗</a> names 14 contribution roles. It describes who did what; the target journal’s rules still determine who qualifies as an author.</p>
          <div class="credit-grid">{creditRoles.map(([en]) => <span>{en}</span>)}</div>
          <p class="takeaway"><strong>Example:</strong> Mei — Conceptualization, Methodology, Writing – original draft; Ravi — Investigation, Data curation, Writing – review &amp; editing. Determine authorship and author order separately under the journal’s criteria.</p>
        </div>
        <div data-language="zh" hidden lang="zh-Hant">
          <h2>CRediT說明論文背後的實際工作</h2>
          <p class="source-context"><a href="https://credit.niso.org/contributor-roles-defined/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">NISO的CRediT分類法 ↗</a>列出14種貢獻角色，用來說明誰做了甚麼；作者資格仍須依目標期刊的規定判斷。</p>
          <div class="credit-grid">{creditRoles.map(([en, zh]) => <span><strong>{en}</strong><small>{zh}</small></span>)}</div>
          <p class="takeaway"><strong>例子：</strong>Mei：研究構思、研究方法、初稿撰寫；Ravi：研究執行、資料整理、審閱與修訂。作者資格與次序須另依期刊準則判斷。</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="slide" data-title="Integrity in the research record" aria-hidden="true">
      <div class="slide-inner">
        <header class="slide-header"><span class="eyebrow">ALLEA (2023) · violations of research integrity</span></header>
        <div data-language="en">
          <h2>Four ways the research record is distorted</h2>
          <p class="source-context">The <a href="https://allea.org/wp-content/uploads/2023/06/European-Code-of-Conduct-Revised-Edition-2023.pdf" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">ALLEA code ↗</a> identifies fabrication, falsification and plagiarism as research misconduct. It also treats unjustified withholding of results and selective citation as unacceptable practices.</p>
          <div class="integrity-four">
            <article><h3>Fabrication</h3><p>Inventing an interview or response that never occurred.</p></article>
            <article><h3>Falsification</h3><p>Changing a transcript, code or dataset to support a preferred result.</p></article>
            <article><h3>Plagiarism</h3><p>Using another scholar’s words, ideas or materials without proper credit.</p></article>
            <article><h3>Selective reporting</h3><p>Hiding contradictory cases or outcomes so findings appear stronger.</p></article>
          </div>
          <p class="takeaway">Keep a traceable record of design changes, exclusions and analytic choices; report limits and disconfirming evidence.</p>
        </div>
        <div data-language="zh" hidden lang="zh-Hant">
          <h2>研究紀錄被扭曲的四種方式</h2>
          <p class="source-context"><a href="https://allea.org/wp-content/uploads/2023/06/European-Code-of-Conduct-Revised-Edition-2023.pdf" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">ALLEA守則 ↗</a>把捏造、篡改與剽竊列為研究不當行為，亦把無正當理由隱瞞結果及選擇性引用列為不可接受做法。</p>
          <div class="integrity-four">
            <article><h3>捏造</h3><p>虛構從未發生的訪談或回答。</p></article>
            <article><h3>篡改</h3><p>修改逐字稿、編碼或資料集，以支持預期結果。</p></article>
            <article><h3>剽竊</h3><p>使用他人的文字、構想或材料，卻沒有適當註明來源。</p></article>
            <article><h3>選擇性報告</h3><p>隱去相反個案或結果，令研究發現顯得更有力。</p></article>
          </div>
          <p class="takeaway">保留可追溯的設計變更、排除及分析決定；報告研究限制與相反證據。</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="slide" data-title="Journal policies on AI use" aria-hidden="true">
      <div class="slide-inner">
        <header class="slide-header"><span class="eyebrow">Language Testing and Elsevier · AI policies</span></header>
        <div data-language="en">
          <h2>AI disclosure depends on the journal</h2>
          <p class="source-context"><strong>Two publishing sources:</strong> <em>Language Testing</em> has its own <a href="https://journals.sagepub.com/pb-assets/cmscontent/ltj/LTJ%20Author%20guidelines%20on%20genAI_Oct_3_24-1731410134.pdf" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">October 2024 guidance ↗</a>; Elsevier publishes a broader <a href="https://www.elsevier.com/about/policies-and-standards/generative-ai-policies-for-journals" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">journal policy ↗</a> relevant to <em>System</em>. Both keep authors responsible for AI-assisted work.</p>
          <div class="policy-grid">
            <article><span>Language Testing · journal-specific guidance</span><p>Identify the tool, task and purpose. Acknowledge generative AI used for language editing; describe research use in Methods. AI analysis of participants’ qualitative data normally requires consent through ethics review, plus accuracy and privacy checks.</p><a href="https://journals.sagepub.com/pb-assets/cmscontent/ltj/LTJ%20Author%20guidelines%20on%20genAI_Oct_3_24-1731410134.pdf" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Read the journal guidelines ↗</a></article>
            <article><span>System · Elsevier publisher policy</span><p>Declare substantive AI assistance in manuscript preparation in a separate statement; basic spelling and grammar checks are exempt. Explain research-process use in Methods. Verify output and references, protect data, and keep authors accountable.</p><a href="https://www.elsevier.com/about/policies-and-standards/generative-ai-policies-for-journals" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Read the current publisher policy ↗</a></article>
          </div>
          <p class="takeaway">Policies differ and can change. Before submitting, check the target journal’s current wording and protect participant data when using external tools.</p>
        </div>
        <div data-language="zh" hidden lang="zh-Hant">
          <h2>AI披露要求取決於目標期刊</h2>
          <p class="source-context"><strong>兩項出版來源：</strong><em>Language Testing</em>有<a href="https://journals.sagepub.com/pb-assets/cmscontent/ltj/LTJ%20Author%20guidelines%20on%20genAI_Oct_3_24-1731410134.pdf" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">2024年10月的專屬指引 ↗</a>；Elsevier有適用於<em>System</em>等期刊的<a href="https://www.elsevier.com/about/policies-and-standards/generative-ai-policies-for-journals" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">出版社政策 ↗</a>。兩者均要求作者為AI輔助成果負責。</p>
          <div class="policy-grid">
            <article><span>Language Testing · 期刊專屬指引</span><p>說明工具、任務及目的；生成式AI用於語言編輯時在致謝披露，用於研究過程時在方法部分交代。以AI分析參與者的質性資料通常須在倫理審查中取得同意，並核查準確性與私隱風險。</p><a href="https://journals.sagepub.com/pb-assets/cmscontent/ltj/LTJ%20Author%20guidelines%20on%20genAI_Oct_3_24-1731410134.pdf" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">閱讀期刊指引 ↗</a></article>
            <article><span>System · Elsevier出版社政策</span><p>以AI實質協助準備稿件，須作獨立聲明；基本拼寫及文法檢查獲豁免。研究過程中使用AI則在方法部分說明。作者須核查輸出與引文、保護資料並承擔責任。</p><a href="https://www.elsevier.com/about/policies-and-standards/generative-ai-policies-for-journals" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">閱讀現行出版社政策 ↗</a></article>
          </div>
          <p class="takeaway">期刊政策各異，亦可能改變。投稿前查核目標期刊現行要求；使用外部工具時須保護參與者資料。</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="slide" data-title="Published AI disclosure examples" aria-hidden="true">
      <div class="slide-inner">
        <header class="slide-header"><span class="eyebrow">System · published disclosure and correction</span></header>
        <div data-language="en">
          <h2>Published records show disclosure and its limits</h2>
          <p class="source-context">A <em>System</em> article shows a writing-related AI declaration alongside participant protections. A separate <em>System</em> corrigendum shows why AI-suggested references still need independent verification.</p>
          <div class="policy-grid">
            <article><span>System (2025) · writing disclosure</span><h3>Lázaro-Ibarrola et al., young multilingual readers</h3><p>The article declares Talk to Claude for readability and proofreading, followed by author review. Its ethics statement also documents institutional approval, parental consent and children’s choice to participate.</p><a href="https://doi.org/10.1016/j.system.2025.103665" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Inspect the article ↗</a></article>
            <article><span>System (2026) · published correction</span><h3>Lin &amp; Tsou, EMI professional development</h3><p>A corrigendum explains that GPT-4o helped identify references. Several AI-suggested citations were insufficiently verified and needed correction. The authors remained responsible for checking primary sources.</p><a href="https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/pii/S0346251X25003136" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Inspect the corrigendum ↗</a></article>
          </div>
          <p class="takeaway">Identify the tool, purpose, study stage, human checks and data permissions. A declaration makes use visible; verify the output independently.</p>
        </div>
        <div data-language="zh" hidden lang="zh-Hant">
          <h2>已發表紀錄呈現披露及其局限</h2>
          <p class="source-context">一篇<em>System</em>文章同時呈現AI寫作披露與參與者保障；另一篇獨立的<em>System</em>更正聲明則說明，AI建議的文獻仍須由作者獨立核查。</p>
          <div class="policy-grid">
            <article><span>System（2025）· 寫作披露</span><h3>Lázaro-Ibarrola等人的多語兒童閱讀研究</h3><p>文章聲明以Talk to Claude改善可讀性及校對，之後由作者審核。倫理聲明亦交代機構批准、家長同意及兒童可自行決定是否參與。</p><a href="https://doi.org/10.1016/j.system.2025.103665" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">查閱文章 ↗</a></article>
            <article><span>System（2026）· 已發表更正</span><h3>Lin與Tsou的EMI教師發展研究</h3><p>更正聲明指出，GPT-4o曾協助找尋文獻。多項AI建議的引文核查不足，後來須予更正。作者仍須核對原始來源。</p><a href="https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/pii/S0346251X25003136" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">查閱更正聲明 ↗</a></article>
          </div>
          <p class="takeaway">找出工具、目的、研究階段、人工核查及資料使用許可。聲明使AI使用可見；輸出仍須獨立核查。</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

